    "updated_at": "2024-10-22T18:40:55Z",
    "body": "we need to update the optgroup element with it's allowance of the `legend` element.\r\n\r\nsimilar to option where someone can either use text, or label/value attributes - the optgroup should either have a label for the group rendered by the use of the `label` attribute OR by someone using a `legend` element.  \r\n\r\nIf both are defined (label attribute and legend element) one should win out over the other, like what happens with option and the current select > option.  \r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n<select>\r\n  <optgroup label=one>\r\n      <legend>two</legend>\r\n       ...\r\n  </optgroup>\r\n   <option label=A>B</option>\r\n</select>\r\n```\r\n\r\nbased on the way the current select works, for the option the visible label would be \"A\".\r\nIf optgroup were to follow suit, then arguably the legend should be ignored / have a UA style of display none.  personally though, i would rather the label attribute be ignored, and the legend is what is what gets visually rendered / names the optgroup. \r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
