    "body": "related to my [above comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10586#issuecomment-2429931537), this text from the `optgroup` element needs to be updated, since `label` isn't the only way to label an `optgroup` anymore\r\n\r\n>The label attribute must be specified. Its value gives the name of the group, for the purposes of the user interface. User agents should use this attribute's value when labeling the group of [option](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#the-option-element) elements in a [select](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#the-select-element) element.\r\n\r\n\r\nProbably should read something like the following (bolded text being my additions / changes)\r\n\r\n\r\n>**If the `optgroup` does not contain a `legend` element,** the label attribute must be specified. Its value gives the name of the group, for the purposes of the user interface. User agents should use this attribute's value when labeling the group of [option](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#the-option-element) elements in a [select](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#the-select-element) element.\r\n\r\nRe: \"User agents should use this attribute's value...\" I'm actually surprised that wasn't a UA 'must'.  But with the addition of the legend element, this seems like it could be the place to clarify what takes priority if both are declared by the author.",
