    "updated_at": "2024-11-01T19:11:24Z",
    "body": "This PR removes some important(?) context about option use within / outside of a datalist. \r\nfor instance, without mention of datalist, the second condition in the option content model doesn't make sense / doesn't appear to do anything with the text inside of the option:\r\n>If the element has a [label](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#attr-option-label) attribute but no [value](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#attr-option-value) attribute: [Text](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/dom.html#text-content).\r\n\r\nper the above, if i have `<option label=foo>test</option>` with the current select, all browsers use \"foo\" as the visible text. But, per the current spec, this makes more sense because other conditions are for use of option as not a child of a datalist.  If the option is a child of a datalist, that example renders \"test\" as the primary label, and \"foo\" as a sort of sub-text (if rendered at all)... and at least chromium browsers expose that subtext as part of the option...\r\n\r\nbut again, that only works within a datalist, which would be good to point out (unless we want to do similar for options within a select - which could be useful.....)\r\n\r\nAdditionally, testing with the current chromium canary build, following the first content model condition results in no visible label for an option\r\n>If the element has a [label](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#attr-option-label) attribute and a [value](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/form-elements.html#attr-option-value) attribute: [Nothing](https://whatpr.org/html/10586/dom.html#concept-content-nothing).\r\n\r\nso `<option value=foo label=test>` renders as an empty option with the customizable select, but renders \"foo\" as a visible label with the current select.\r\n\r\nif the label attribute is not being used in the customizable select, i think this needs to be clearly stated.  (checking/rechecking the definition for option and the label attribute, i don't see this called out?)\r\n\r\nbut just as importantly, it should also be clear whether new content model allowances are only allowed within options of a styleable select, or if they are allowed for options in a datalist.  the current PR reads as if this is a change for everywhere, and i'm not sure if that's really the intent at this point?\r\n\r\nEdit: we spoke about some of this in OpenUI yesterday, so just wanted to acknowledge what I wrote here is at least going to be partially addressed.\r\n",
