    "updated_at": "2024-11-12T16:25:30Z",
    "body": "> work be done to not render both the text from the label attribute AND the legend - which is what's happening now and seems rather rubbish - especially if someone has to write duplicate / close to duplicate content just so they can put an image into their optgroup label\r\n\r\nThe text in the legend element replaces the text in the label attribute for both rendering and what's exposed to the accessibility tree. The fact that both the label attribute gets rendered when you have a legend is a bug, I'll fix it here: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/378601807",
